Package: uu-remote-for-linux
Version: @VERSION@
Section: net
Priority: optional
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: UU Remote for Linux Contributors
Conflicts: uuyc-linux-controller
Replaces: uuyc-linux-controller
Depends: bash, ca-certificates, coreutils, curl, ethtool, findutils, gir1.2-appindicator3-0.1, gir1.2-gtk-3.0, iproute2, libglib2.0-bin, libx11-6, libxtst6, network-manager, policykit-1, python3, python3-gi, systemd, tar, util-linux, xdg-desktop-portal
Recommends: wine (>= 11.1) | winehq-stable (>= 11.1) | winehq-devel (>= 11.1) | winehq-staging (>= 11.1), libnotify-bin, zenity, pciutils
Suggests: vainfo
Description: unofficial UU Remote compatibility wrapper for Linux
 Runs the official NetEase UU Remote Windows client in an isolated Wine prefix
 with native Linux integration for controller and X11 or experimental Wayland
 controlled-host workflows. The proprietary upstream installer is downloaded
 from NetEase on first setup and is not included in this package.
